- Scope: Disposition of `MQClientAPIFactory` protected subclass hooks

## Finding

Pinned Java declares protected `init()` and `createAndStart(String)`.
The constructor invokes `init`; `start()` calls `createAndStart` once per
pool slot. The pinned client source/tests contain no subclass of the factory;
the only `createAndStart` callsite is the base `start` loop. The base
initialization and slot creation map to Rust factory `build` and `start`.
Remoting-client construction and refresh scheduling are separately injectable
through Rust's public creator and scheduler adapters.

These are protected override points rather than Java-public client methods or
settings. Rust has no Java-style subclass dispatch. The parity contract covers
the direct public factory surface, not third-party Java subclass source
compatibility. This resolves the earlier open scope review without claiming
that Rust can host a Java subclass.

